# interplay_memlive_held_first_use: An exec that fills a shared buffer made before (S), and a shared buffer (N), a private buffer (P), a two-page private heap with a buffer at its second page (H) and a texture (X) that no exec has named yet, waits on the gate while the guest points each one's leaves at other pages (for the heap only its second page). Released, the exec makes N, P, H and X from the table as it is then, in every setup: N's fill lands in its new page; P, H and X are paged from their new pages (a copy out shows the new bytes). S, live, fills its old page.
